# Pre-launch audit findings

## CONFIRMED — CRITICAL

### C1. Public `GET /api/merchants/:id` leaks passwordHash + all secrets
- File: server/routes.ts:917 (no `authenticateToken`)
- `storage.getMerchant` (storage.ts:1729) = `select().from(merchants)` → all 52 cols
- Route returns `{...merchant, paymentUrl, qrCodeUrl}` — no field stripping
- LIVE PROOF: `/api/merchants/22` returns `passwordHash` (60-char bcrypt), `nzbn`, `gstNumber`. bank*/windcaveApiKey/coinbase*/resetToken/verificationToken all present-as-keys (null on 22, populated on real merchants).
- Impact: enumerate sequential ids → harvest every bcrypt hash (offline crack) + payment-processor API keys + live resetToken (→ account takeover).
- Fix: sanitize merchant before returning on all PUBLIC endpoints. Central `publicMerchant(m)` allow-list serializer.

## Sibling leaks checked
- checkout/resolve (6096): SAFE — hand-picks merchantName + customLogoUrl only. Correct pattern to mirror.
- active-transaction (1004): returns raw `transaction` (not merchant). Check tx PII later (LOW).
- admin/merchants (3752) + admin/merchants/:id (3766): return full merchant incl passwordHash to admin UI — LOW (admin-gated) but should strip.

## CONFIRMED — HIGH / MEDIUM

### C2. IDOR write: PUT /api/merchants/:id/business-details (routes.ts:4200)
- No authenticateToken, no ownership check. Only gate = merchant is email-verified.
- Anyone can overwrite ANY verified/active merchant's businessName, director, contactEmail, contactPhone, gstNumber, businessAddress, nzbn by id.
- contactEmail overwrite = comms interception vector. Severity: HIGH (data integrity / fraud).
- Nuance: this is an onboarding step (pre-login, no JWT yet) so can't simply require auth; needs onboarding-session binding OR require auth once status=active.

### C3. Cross-tenant SSE leak: GET /api/merchants/:id/events (routes.ts:4320)
- No auth. Subscriber picks any merchantId; broadcastToStone / crypto handlers push FULL `transaction` + `cryptoTransaction` objects (amounts, item names, customer data, crypto addresses).
- Attacker subscribes to competitor merchant id → live sales feed. Severity: MEDIUM (BI/PII leak + connection-accumulation DoS).

### C4. Refund double-submit → over-refund (routes.ts:4550)
- Authenticated + ownership-checked (good). But check-then-act: reads refundableAmount (4587), checks (4589), moves money at Windcave (4617), updates totals (4640) — no lock/atomic guard.
- Two concurrent refunds / double-clicked Refund button both pass the check → double money out. merchantReference includes Date.now() so Windcave won't dedupe. updateTransactionAfterRefund is read-modify-write (storage.ts:722) so totals also lose an increment.
- Severity: MEDIUM (merchant self-inflicted; realistic via UI double-submit). Fix: atomic conditional decrement of refundableAmount BEFORE Windcave call, or idempotency key.

## VERIFIED CLEAN (checked, no bug)
- Split payments: atomicClaimSplitShare (storage.ts:3215) — single atomic UPDATE, session-dedupe array guard, count<splitCount guard, settled guard, RETURNING post-increment. Correct.
- Windcave idempotency: stable xId threaded through all retries (windcave.ts:428,493,118,180). 2026-07-07 fix intact.
- Crypto confirm (routes.ts:2277): gated to non-production (404 in prod). Safe.
- GST (shared/trades-gst.ts): integer-cents, correct inclusive-extraction & exclusive-add, deposit clamped. No rounding bug.
